{"title":"Career Roadmap · Optical Design Engineer","role":"Optical Design Engineer","summary":"An Optical Design Engineer designs, analyzes, simulates, prototypes, tests, and optimizes optical systems used in areas such as cameras, imaging systems, lasers, fiber-optic communications, sensors, LiDAR, displays, medical instruments, semiconductor equipment, aerospace systems, and industrial instrumentation.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Optoelectronics / Photonics Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Optical Design Engineer designs, analyzes, simulates, prototypes, tests, and optimizes optical systems used in areas such as cameras, imaging systems, lasers, fiber-optic communications, sensors, LiDAR, displays, medical instruments, semiconductor equipment, aerospace systems, and industrial instrumentation."},{"type":"p","text":"For an Optoelectronics/Photonics graduate, the strongest profile combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Geometrical Optics","Physical Optics","Electromagnetics","Optical Design Software","Optomechanics","Optoelectronics","Simulation","Experimental Testing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The role is highly multidisciplinary. A strong engineer should understand not only how light propagates, but also how optical components, detectors, electronics, mechanical structures, thermal effects, coatings and software interact in a real product."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Tech + Photonics Foundation"},{"text":"Optics, electromagnetics, optical simulation, instrumentation"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Optical Design Engineer / Junior Optical Engineer"},{"text":"Lens design, optical simulation, testing and tolerancing"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior Optica